# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 237-241 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, 2026-09-25): the garment spread — R. Ishmael's parable, R. Akiva's
# plotting witnesses, R. Eliezer b. Jacob's letter (237); the man not the minor, the lashes, the money, Tyrian silver, the father's hundred, the adult and the
# convert, all Israel's virgins, he drinks from his pot, all his days, the levir (238); the true charge, no witnesses to refute, the father's door (239); in the
# presence of the city, the stone and the stones, folly, the priest's daughter's analogy, the evil-doers purged (240); by witnesses, the betrothed bedded, the
# unspecified death is strangling, Herod's deed, those who come after, the minors (241). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(237, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SPREAD THE GARMENT" (22:17) — THEY MAKE THE WORDS CLEAR AS A GARMENT; ONE OF THE THINGS R. ISHMAEL EXPOUNDED FROM THE TORAH AS A PARABLE — "IF THE SUN ROSE ON HIM" (Exodus 22:2): DOES THE SUN RISE ON HIM ALONE? AS THE SUN IS PEACE TO THE WORLD, SO IF HE KNEW THE THIEF WAS AT PEACE WITH HIM AND KILLED HIM — LIABLE; "ON HIS STAFF" (Exodus 21:19) — ON HIS HEALTH; SO "THEY SPREAD THE GARMENT". The head row of piska 237 ({SP_(237, 1, "יחורו", "דברים", "כשמלה")} "they make the words clear as a garment"; {SP_(237, 1, "במשל")} "as a parable"): THE GARMENT A FIGURE — the evidence made plain, not the cloth itself; R. Ishmael\'s three parables of the law (Mekhilta Neziqin 6) — the compile reads "the garment" as the proof\'s clarity. Fresh.')
srow(237, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA SAYS: "THEY SPREAD THE GARMENT BEFORE THE ELDERS OF THE CITY" — THE HUSBAND\'S WITNESSES ARE FOUND PLOTTING; "THEY SPREAD THE GARMENT" — THIS ONE\'S WITNESSES AND THAT ONE\'S COME AND SPEAK BEFORE THE ELDERS. ({SP_(237, 2, "נמצאו", "עדי", "הבעל", "זוממים")} "the husband\'s witnesses are found plotting"): THE PLOTTING WITNESSES NAMED — 19:18-19\'s law inside the bride\'s case (236:1\'s reading made explicit); the two parties\' witnesses before the court. Fresh.')
srow(237, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER B. JACOB SAYS: THE WORDS AS THEY ARE WRITTEN. ({SP_(237, 3, "דברים", "ככתבם")} "the words as written"): the garment literal — three readings of one clause (the parable, the witnesses, the letter); the compile carries the witnesses\' arm with the cloth as evidence. Fresh.')
srow(238, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE ELDERS OF THAT CITY TAKE THE MAN" (22:18) — AND NOT THE MINOR. The head row of piska 238 ({SP_(238, 1, "ולא", "את", "הקטן")} "and not the minor"): the slanderer\'s age condition — an adult (245:1 the rapist\'s twin). Fresh.')
srow(238, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND CHASTISE HIM" — WITH LASHES. ({SP_(238, 2, "במכות")} "with lashes"): the chastisement the court\'s lashes — the first of the slanderer\'s two penalties. Fresh.')
srow(238, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND FINE HIM" (22:19) — MONEY. ({SP_(238, 3, "ממון")} "money"): the second penalty — lashes and money together for the slanderer (the one case of both, Makkot 1:3\'s ground). Fresh.')
srow(238, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"A HUNDRED OF SILVER" — TYRIAN SILVER. ({SP_(238, 4, "כסף", "צורי")} "Tyrian silver"): THE COIN\'S STANDARD — the fine in Tyrian silver, the heavy coin (Onkelos "a hundred sela of silver" — the ink\'s find 15); the compile\'s money PARAMETER. Fresh.')
srow(238, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND GIVE TO THE GIRL\'S FATHER" — THAT THEY BE HIS. ({SP_(238, 5, "שיהו", "שלו")} "that they be his"): the fine the father\'s property. Fresh.')
srow(238, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND GIVE TO THE GIRL\'S FATHER" — AND NOT TO THE ADULT WOMAN\'S FATHER; "TO THE GIRL\'S FATHER" — EXCLUDING A CONVERT CONCEIVED NOT IN HOLINESS AND BORN IN HOLINESS, WHO HAS NO HUNDRED OF SILVER. ({SP_(238, 6, "ולא", "לאבי", "הבוגרת")} "and not to the adult woman\'s father"; {SP_(238, 6, "פרט", "לגיורת")} "excluding a convert"): THE AGE PARAMETER — the na\'arah (a girl of twelve to twelve and a half) against the bogeret (the adult) — and the convert\'s exclusion (Ketubot 4:3 the answer sheet). Fresh.')
srow(238, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR HE BROUGHT AN EVIL NAME" — NOT ON HER ALONE, BUT ON ALL THE VIRGINS OF ISRAEL. ({SP_(238, 7, "על", "כל", "בתולות", "ישראל")} "on all the virgins of Israel"): the slander\'s reach the penalty\'s ground (240:3 the bride\'s twin). Fresh.')
srow(238, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SHE SHALL BE HIS WIFE" — HE DRINKS FROM HIS OWN POT: EVEN LAME, EVEN BLIND, EVEN SMITTEN WITH BOILS; A LEWD MATTER FOUND IN HER, OR SHE IS UNFIT TO ENTER ISRAEL — MAY HE KEEP HER? "SHE SHALL BE HIS WIFE" — A WIFE FIT FOR HIM. ({SP_(238, 8, "ששותה", "בעציצו")} "that he drinks from his pot"; {SP_(238, 8, "אשה", "הראויה", "לו")} "a wife fit for him"): THE FORCED MARRIAGE and its one exception — the forbidden union (Ketubot 3:5 the answer sheet); the compile\'s status "his wife, undivorceable" with the fitness condition. Fresh.')
srow(238, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE MAY NOT SEND HER AWAY ALL HIS DAYS" — EVEN AFTER TIME. ({SP_(238, 9, "ואפלו", "לאחר", "זמן")} "even after time"): the bar permanent. Fresh.')
srow(238, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'["ALL HIS DAYS"] — HE SENDS HER TO THE LEVIR. ({SP_(238, 10, "משלחה", "הוא", "ליבם")} "he sends her to the levir"): the one release — death without a son sends her to the husband\'s brother (25:5 ahead; 245:7 the twin close): the levirate\'s pointer inside chapter 22. Fresh.')
srow(239, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF THE THING WAS TRUE" (22:20) — ONLY IN HER NATURAL WAY? UNNATURAL FROM "WAS"; MIGHT I INCLUDE INTERCOURSE IN ANOTHER PLACE? "THIS". The head row of piska 239 ({SP_(239, 1, "שלא", "כדרכה", "מנין")} "not in her way — whence?"): the charge\'s substance widened and bounded by two words. Fresh.')
srow(239, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"NO TOKENS WERE FOUND FOR THE GIRL" — THERE ARE NO WITNESSES TO REFUTE HIS WITNESSES. ({SP_(239, 2, "אין", "עדים", "להזם", "עדיו", "של", "זה")} "there are no witnesses to refute this one\'s witnesses"): 236:1\'s mirror — the "tokens" are witnesses on both arms; the true charge is the unrefuted testimony. Fresh.')
srow(239, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"BRING THE GIRL OUT TO HER FATHER\'S DOOR" (22:21) — A FATHER AND A FATHER\'S DOOR ONLY? A DOOR AND NO FATHER — "BRING THE GIRL OUT" ANYWHERE; WHY "HER FATHER\'S DOOR"? A COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(239, 3, "פתח", "בית", "אב", "ואין", "לה", "אב", "מנין")} "a father\'s door and no father — whence?"; {SP_(239, 3, "מצוה")} "a commandment"): the place of execution preferred, not conditioned (Ketubot 4:3) — the orphan bride stoned all the same. Fresh.')
srow(240, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ALL THE MEN OF HER CITY STONE HER" (22:21) — DO ALL THE MEN OF HER CITY STONE HER? IN THE PRESENCE OF ALL THE MEN OF HER CITY. The head row of piska 240 ({SP_(240, 1, "במעמד", "כל", "אנשי", "עירה")} "in the presence of all the men of her city"): the stoning public — 220:1\'s words for the rebellious son. Fresh.')
srow(240, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH STONES" — MANY STONES? "WITH A STONE" (Leviticus 20:2); ONE STONE? "WITH STONES" — IF SHE DIED NOT BY THE FIRST, LET HER DIE BY THE SECOND. ({SP_(240, 2, "אם", "לא", "מתה", "בראשונה", "תמות", "בשניה")} "if she did not die by the first she dies by the second"): THE STONING\'S PROCEDURE — the stone and the stones (Sifrei Numbers 114; Sanhedrin 6:4 the answer sheet\'s rite); the compile\'s stoning cell reused. Fresh.')
srow(240, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR SHE COMMITTED FOLLY IN ISRAEL" — NOT HERSELF ALONE SHE DISGRACED, BUT ALL THE VIRGINS OF ISRAEL. ({SP_(240, 3, "כל", "בתולות", "ישראל")} "all the virgins of Israel"): the folly\'s reach (238:7\'s twin on the other side). Fresh.')
srow(240, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO PLAY THE HARLOT IN HER FATHER\'S HOUSE" — "HER FATHER" HERE AND "HER FATHER" THERE (Leviticus 21:9): AS THERE HARLOTRY UNDER A HUSBAND\'S BOND, SO HERE. ({SP_(240, 4, "זנות", "עם", "זיקת", "הבעל")} "harlotry with a husband\'s bond"): THE PRIEST\'S DAUGHTER\'S ANALOGY (I2) — the bride\'s sin is adultery while betrothed, not unchastity before (Sifra Emor the parallel); the compile\'s predicate. Fresh.')
srow(240, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND PURGE THE EVIL FROM YOUR MIDST" — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(240, 5, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): THE PURGE FORMULA\'S SIXTH SEAT of nine read as persons (155:9\'s words, 86:2 the first) — the effect on the doer. Fresh.')
srow(241, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IF A MAN BE FOUND" (22:22) — BY WITNESSES; "LYING WITH A WOMAN" — ANY LYING; "MARRIED TO A HUSBAND" — TO INCLUDE ONE BEDDED IN HER FATHER\'S HOUSE WHILE STILL BETROTHED. The head row of piska 241 ({SP_(241, 1, "בעדים")} "by witnesses"; {SP_(241, 1, "ועדין", "היא", "ארוסה")} "and she is still betrothed"): the adulterer\'s three conditions — witnesses, any act, the married or betrothed woman. Fresh.')
srow(241, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SHALL DIE" — THE UNSPECIFIED DEATH SAID IN THE TORAH: STRANGLING. ({SP_(241, 2, "בחנק")} "by strangling"): THE DEFAULT DEATH — where the Torah names no mode, strangulation (Sanhedrin 7:1-3\'s rule; 155:1\'s precedent for the rebellious elder); the adulterer\'s mode the compile\'s parameter. Fresh.')
srow(241, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"BOTH OF THEM" — AND NOT THOSE WHO DO HEROD\'S DEED. ({SP_(241, 3, "מעשה", "הירודס")} "Herod\'s deed"): the dead woman no adultery — the living pair the condition (the Talmud\'s tale of Herod, Bava Batra 3b, not opened). Fresh.')
srow(241, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'WHEN IT SAYS "EVEN BOTH" — TO INCLUDE THOSE WHO COME AFTER THEM. ({SP_(241, 4, "לרבות", "הבאים", "מאחריהם")} "to include those who come after them"): the later partners liable too — "even" the widening word. Fresh.')
srow(241, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE MAN LYING WITH THE WOMAN" — EVEN THOUGH SHE IS A MINOR. ({SP_(241, 5, "שהיא", "קטנה")} "that she is a minor"): the man liable for a married minor. Fresh.')
srow(241, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE WOMAN" — EVEN THOUGH SHE WAS BEDDED BY A MINOR. ({SP_(241, 6, "שנבעלה", "לקטן")} "that she was bedded by a minor"): the woman liable though the man is not — the two arms of "both". Fresh.')
srow(241, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND PURGE THE EVIL" — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(241, 7, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): the formula\'s seventh seat, "from Israel" (17:12 its other) — the effect on the pair. Fresh.')
